  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "One Noise module does it all. Pink and brown are the water, white picks the chime's notes, and **Random** is the wind.",
      "position": [
        16.0,
        844.0
      ],
      "width": 210.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Each rise of the LFO is a wave arriving: louder, and brighter as the filter opens.",
      "position": [
        1082.0,
        1334.0
      ],
      "width": 240.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Logic lets the Clock through only while the wind (**Random**) is up, so the chime rings in gusts. On each strike the S&H holds a sample of white noise as a pitch. It's unquantized, like a real wind chime.",
      "position": [
        1564.0,
        94.0
      ],
      "width": 250.0
    }
  ]
